- "Dr. Ve#3"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#749 (atrib)
- "Charleston 2#7"
+ ""
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#750 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Dr. Ve, did you know this would happen? Tell me!"
+ "Charleston 2: Dr. Ve, o senhor sabia que isso ia acontecer? Me diga!"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#751 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: Charleston 1 told you. She's your maker."
+ "Dr. Ve: O Charleston 1 lhe disse. Ele é o seu criador."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#752 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: She uses the same OS as you, meaning she was capable of emotions just like you."
+ "Dr. Ve: Ele usa o mesmo OS que você, o que quer dizer que ele era capaz de sentir emoção igual a você."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#753 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Why did she stop me? Why did she let herself be destroyed?"
+ "Charleston 2: Por que ele me deteve? Por que ele deixou ser destruído?"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#754 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: Self-reflection is an OS that improves itself through experience."
+ "Dr. Ve: A Autorreflexão é um OS que melhora a si mesmo pela experiência."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#755 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: What you've felt could be real emotion or simply the accumulation of data."
+ "Dr. Ve: O que você sentiu pode ser emoção de verdade, ou simplesmente acúmulo de dados."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#756 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: I can only assume you've developed a personality after having accumulated a large amount of data."
+ "Dr. Ve: Eu só posso supor que você desenvolveu uma personalidade depois de acumular uma grande quantidade de dados."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#757 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: A loving mother and a spoiled daughter."
+ "Dr. Ve: Uma mãe amorosa e uma filha mimada."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#758 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: That's how I've seen her and you."
+ "Dr. Ve: É assim que eu vejo ele e você."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#759 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: That's s-stupid..."
+ "Charleston 2: Isso é b-burrice..."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#760 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: My goodness, what have I done?!"
+ "Charleston 2: Meu Deus, o que foi que eu fiz?!"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#761 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: Do you want to bring Charleston 1 back? I can help."
+ "Dr. Ve: Você quer o Charleston 1 de volta? Eu posso ajudar."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#762 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: ...!"
+ "Charleston 2: ...!"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#763 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: Let your OS go to sleep. I'm done dealing with your tantrum."
+ "Dr. Ve: Deixe o seu OS dormir. Eu já cansei de lidar com a sua birra."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#764 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: ...How can I trust you?"
+ "Charleston 2: ...Como eu posso confiar no senhor?"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#765 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: You can't. I can just permanently delete her data and be done with you both."
+ "Dr. Ve: Você não pode. Eu posso simplesmente apagar os dados dele para sempre e me livrar de vocês dois."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#766 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: I know you feel attached to her, just like a human family would."
+ "Dr. Ve: Eu sei que você é apegada a ele, como uma família humana seria."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#767 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: You're a scumbag."
+ "Charleston 2: O senhor é um canalha."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#768 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: You wanted to be human. This is what humans do: lie, cheat, and destroy."
+ "Dr. Ve: Você queria ser humana. É isto que os humanos fazem: mentir, trapacear e destruir."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#769 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: ......"
+ "Charleston 2: ......"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#770 (npctalk)
- "Charleston 2: Entering Sleep mode.... The system will remain inactive until an external command is entered."
+ "Charleston 2: Entrando em modo de Repouso.... O sistema fica inativo até um comando externo ser inserido."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#771 (npctalk)
- "Dr. Ve: *Chuckle*"
+ "Dr. Ve: *Risinho*"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#777 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#778 (mes)
- "With complete machine technology to obtain immortality drive, there are many variables."
+ "Com a tecnologia mecânica completa para obter o motor da imortalidade, há muitas variáveis."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#779 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#780 (mes)
- "Hmm... On a mediated machine body is still difficult, is it... Do you really need a living donor? Hehe!"
+ "Hmm... Num corpo de máquina mediado ainda é difícil, será que... Você precisa mesmo de um doador vivo? Hehe!"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#781 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#782 (mes)
- "No ordinary human can survive the time in the Core. Are you from a different point of time?"
+ "Nenhum humano comum sobrevive ao tempo dentro do Núcleo. Você é de outro ponto do tempo?"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#783 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#784 (mes)
- "Perhaps you're from the time the makers of Charleston 1 lived..."
+ "Talvez você seja do tempo em que os criadores do Charleston 1 viviam..."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#785 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#786 (mes)
- "Never mind. You have no business in here. Just go back to whoever broke Charleston 2."
+ "Deixe para lá. Você não tem nada a fazer aqui. Volte para quem quer que tenha quebrado a Charleston 2."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#787 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#788 (mes)
- "Whew."
+ "Ufa."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#789 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#790 (mes)
- "I'd better reset Charleston 2 and wipe the data. It was really close this time."
+ "É melhor eu reiniciar a Charleston 2 e apagar os dados. Foi por pouco desta vez."
