- "Another Charleston 2?"
+ "Outra Charleston 2?"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#803 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#804 (mes)
- "Charleston 2's OS has improved on its own like a living brain."
+ "O OS da Charleston 2 melhorou por conta própria, como um cérebro vivo."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#805 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#806 (mes)
- "Every time Charleston 2 comes back to life, though in a different machine, she's more intelligent, more sensible, and more troublesome."
+ "Toda vez que a Charleston 2 volta à vida, mesmo numa máquina diferente, ela fica mais inteligente, mais sensível e mais problemática."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#807 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#808 (mes)
- "There's nothing you or I can do. We'll have to wait until Charleston 1 repairs herself."
+ "Não há nada que você ou eu possamos fazer. Vamos ter que esperar até o Charleston 1 se consertar."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#809 (mes)
- "Dr. Ve sighs and writes down something."
+ "O Dr. Ve suspira e anota alguma coisa."
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#810 (mes)
- "[Dr. Ve]"
+ "[Dr. Ve]"
#: npc/re/instances/CharlestonCrisis.txt#811 (mes)
- "By the way, there are too many variables to achieve immortality through mechanical engineering."
+ "Aliás, há variáveis demais para alcançar a imortalidade pela engenharia mecânica."
